            {
              "id": "16eee4a3-5655-4cac-9aca-164581780e98",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Queer Game Studies</strong></em> is a collection of essays edited by Bonnie Ruberg &amp; Adrienne Shaw, published by University Of Minnesota Press, March 28, 2017."
            },
            {
              "id": "68621b57-ab8a-4ab2-9e34-96d5dea279ab",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "cabaf188-32ef-4b35-9118-e4c80062a16b",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Video games have developed into a rich, growing field at many top universities, but they have rarely been considered from a queer perspective. Immersion in new worlds, video games seem to offer the perfect opportunity to explore the alterity that queer culture longs for, but often sexism and discrimination in gamer culture steal the spotlight. </em>Queer Game Studies<em> provides a welcome corrective, revealing the capacious albeit underappreciated communities that are making, playing, and studying queer games.<br><br>These in-depth, diverse, and accessible essays use queerness to challenge the ideas that have dominated gaming discussions. Demonstrating the centrality of LGBTQ issues to the gamer world, they establish an alternative lens for examining this increasingly important culture. </em>Queer Game Studies <em>covers important subjects such as the representation of queer bodies, the </em><a href=\"#/playing-with-the-guys\"><em>casual misogyny</em></a><em> prevalent in video games, the need for greater diversity in gamer culture, and reading popular games like </em>Bayonetta, Mass Effect<em>, and </em>Metal Gear Solid<em> from a queer perspective.<br><br>Perfect for both everyday readers and instructors looking to add diversity to their courses, </em>Queer Game Studies<em> is the ideal introduction to the vast and vibrant realm of queer gaming.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "510e0780-15d1-45c2-8f31-40be1b4c2ff2",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
